{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA `rebar` command run from a linked git worktree reads the **main checkout's** `rebar.toml`, so keys only that file has (here a stale `llm.overlap_drain`) warn against the worktree, and config meant for the caller came from the wrong file. Evidence (stack traces, measured runs, history) is in the comments.\n\n**Part 1 — landed in 141da5419a3 (Gerrit 3206):** `push_tickets_branch` now resolves `sync.push` from the caller's repo root, and first-run linking (`_main_worktree_tracker`, `src/rebar/_commands/init.py`) reads only the main checkout's `tracker.dir` via `config.peer_tracker_dir` (`src/rebar/config.py`). Tests: `tests/unit/test_worktree_config_root.py`.\n\n**Part 2 — this plan's remaining work.** The live check after Part 1 still warned (1 of 3 first-run `show`s, and on a write). 5 call sites read the *shared store's* branch and remote from the store's parent (the main checkout) through a full validating `load_config`:\n- `src/rebar/_store/sync.py:218`, `:220` — `reconverge` (`tickets_branch`/`tickets_remote`), reached from `show` via `ensure_fresh`.\n- `src/rebar/_store/push.py:120` — `_require_s3_helper_for_configured_remote` (`tickets_remote`).\n- `src/rebar/_store/push.py:193`, `:194` — `push_tickets_branch` destination (`tickets_branch`/`tickets_remote`).\n\nTheir root is intended (`sync.py` marks them `repo-root-ok: branch/remote of the STORE's own git repo`; 6b96fd3d148 chose the main repo for the push destination; the async push child runs at `store_repo_root`, `src/rebar/_proc.py:90`). The defect is validating the whole file to read 2 keys.\n\n## Approach\n\nSame principle as Part 1: read only the keys the caller needs from the store's parent, keeping their validation. In `src/rebar/config.py` add `store_tickets_branch(root)` and `store_tickets_remote(root)`:\n1. A bound operation snapshot for that root wins, as in `_config_value` (`_bound_snapshot_for_root`, `src/rebar/config.py:122`).\n2. Otherwise precedence mirrors `load_config` for one key: schema default (`TrackerConfig.branch` / `SyncConfig.remote`, `src/rebar/_config_schema.py`) < raw user/project layers from `raw_layers(root)` (`src/rebar/_config_sources.py:209`, no `coerce_sparse`, so no unknown-key warnings) < `env_overrides()` (`REBAR_TRACKER_BRANCH` / `REBAR_SYNC_REMOTE`) < process `--config` overrides (`_CLI_OVERRIDES`).\n3. The chosen value is validated with `_as_git_ref` / `_as_git_remote` (`src/rebar/_config_coercion.py:243`, `:267`), which raise `ConfigError`; a non-table section also raises `ConfigError`. An unreadable TOML still raises `ConfigError` from `_parse_toml`. So all 5 sites keep their existing `except ConfigError` fail-closed paths.\n\nOne private raw-layer reader (the layer WALK only: it returns the last raw value, or raises `ConfigError` for a non-table section) is shared with Part 1's `_raw_tracker_dir`, so the walk has one home. Error policy stays per caller: `store_tickets_branch`/`store_tickets_remote` propagate `ConfigError` (fail closed), while `_raw_tracker_dir` keeps its existing fall-back-to-default. The 5 sites switch to the new functions; their roots do not change.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/config.py` — `store_tickets_branch`, `store_tickets_remote`, shared raw-layer reader.\n- `src/rebar/_store/sync.py` — lines 218, 220.\n- `src/rebar/_store/push.py` — lines 120, 193, 194.\n- `tests/unit/test_worktree_config_root.py` — new cases.\n- Tests that steer these 5 sites by monkeypatching `config.tickets_branch`/`tickets_remote` move their patch target to the new names, otherwise they would silently resolve real defaults: `tests/unit/test_push_strict.py`, `tests/unit/test_push_strict_happy.py`, `tests/unit/test_push_expected_contention_quiet.py`, `tests/unit/test_cas_backoff_refetch_baldish.py`, `tests/integration/test_s3_preflight.py`, `tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py`.\n- `docs/env-vars.md` — regenerated only if `gen_env_registry --check` cites shifted `config.py` lines.\n\n## Testing\n\nIn `tests/unit/test_worktree_config_root.py` (main repo + linked worktree; main `rebar.toml` has an unknown `[llm]` key and `[sync] remote = \"mainremote\"`, `[tracker] branch = \"mainbranch\"`):\n- Sync read: `sync.reconverge(<main tracker>)` with `sync._coordinated_fetch` spied — the refspec names `mainremote`/`mainbranch` and no `rebar.config` \"unknown key\" record is logged.\n- Write: `push.push_tickets_branch(<main tracker>)` with `push._git` spied — the push names `mainremote` and `HEAD:mainbranch`, with no unknown-key record.\n- Invalid values still refused: main `[tracker] branch = \"bad..branch\"` makes `push_tickets_branch(..., strict=True)` raise `PushDeliveryError` reason `invalid-destination`; main `[sync] remote = \"-bad\"` makes `store_tickets_remote` raise `ConfigError`.\n- Precedence: `REBAR_SYNC_REMOTE` overrides the file value.\n\nRegression: `pytest tests/unit/test_worktree_config_root.py tests/unit/test_push_strict.py tests/unit/test_push_strict_happy.py tests/unit/test_push_expected_contention_quiet.py tests/unit/test_cas_backoff_refetch_baldish.py tests/integration/test_s3_preflight.py tests/integration/test_s3_doctor.py tests/unit/test_sync_remote_config.py tests/unit/test_relocated_store_repo_root.py tests/unit/test_gate_store_freshness.py -m \"\"`, then `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A ticket-resolving command run from a linked worktree emits no warning about the main checkout's config. Checked by: after Part 2 lands, from a fresh worktree at `origin/main`, 3 first-run `rebar show nosophobic-zebraic-waterbug` runs (tracker symlink removed before each) and 3 ticket writes print 0 lines naming `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/rebar.toml`.\n- [ ] Regression tests pin the behaviour with a temp main repo and a linked worktree with differing `rebar.toml` values: first-run linking honours the main `tracker.dir` without warning; a write uses the worktree's `sync.push`; sync reads and writes take the store's branch/remote without unknown-key warnings; invalid branch/remote values are still refused. Checked by: `pytest tests/unit/test_worktree_config_root.py` passes; against 141da5419a3 its Part 2 no-warning cases and `store_tickets_*` cases fail, while its refusal cases pass on both (they pin behaviour that must not change).\n- [ ] Existing push, sync and init behaviour is unchanged. Checked by: the Testing regression command passes, and `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0.\n- [ ] The MCP `stale-store` divergence is recorded as a separate cause on topnotch-brazen-slug. Checked by: a `relates_to` link to it and a note on it citing the `.git`-is-a-directory evidence."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793538064296328001,"uuid":"e7f2d71b-90f3-4f7b-98ed-c58e127f3684"}